
Scenario: userLoginAndBrowseMissionsIntegrationTest | Verifies that a regular user can log in, browse missions, and view a mission listing through the terminal interface.
GIVEN an existing user named alice with a valid password and regular-user access, and a mission named Operation Eclipse
WHEN alice logs in, selects Browse Missions, views the mission list, and returns to the main menu
THEN the application exits successfully and the terminal output contains Login successful., Browse missions, and Operation Eclipse.

Scenario: adminCreatesFacilityIntegrationTest | Verifies that an administrator can log in and create a facility through the terminal interface.
GIVEN an existing administrator account and a facility named Headquarters with abbreviation HQ
WHEN the administrator logs in, selects Facilities, chooses to add a facility, and enters the facility details
THEN the application exits successfully, the terminal output contains the login confirmation, facility prompts, and Headquarters, and the data store's addFacility method is called.

Scenario: userChangesPasswordIntegrationTest | Verifies that a regular user can log in and change their password through the terminal interface.
GIVEN an existing regular user named alice with the password oldPassword
WHEN alice logs in, selects the change-password option, and enters newPassword as both the new password and confirmation
THEN the application exits successfully, the terminal output contains the login confirmation, New password:, and Password changed, and the user manager's changePassword method is called with alice, newPassword, and newPassword.
